{"title":"Topicwise Test-15 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 DA Artificial Intelligence-1","fileName":"054_Topicwise Test-15 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 DA Artificial Intelligence-1.html","branch":"DATA SCIENCE AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Data Science and AI","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following is evaluation function in the A* technique?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Heuristic function.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Path cost from the start node to current node.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Path cost from the start node to current node and heuristic cost.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Average of path cost from the start node to the current node and heuristic cost.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/4783c79de7811a7275bbbbfa9313ea45db983060.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following should be considered to increase the performance of heuristic search?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Quality of nodes.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Quality of heuristic function.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> A simple form of nodes.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of the above</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)<br />\n A good heuristic function provides accurate cost estimates to goal, improving search efficiency by effectively guiding the search.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n What is the negation of the statement: “For every student, there exists a course they dislike”?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> There exists a student who dislikes every course.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Every student dislikes every course.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> There exists a course that every student likes.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Every student likes every course.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)<br />\n &ldquo;There exists a course that every student likes&rdquo;. The negation of a universal quantifier &forall; is an existential quantifier &exist;, and vice-versa.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following statements is/are correct regarding adversarial?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Estimate of the utility of a node.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> To calculate the depth of the search tree.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> To implement alpha-beta pruning.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following is the correct syntax for expressing that “not all humans are immortal” in first-order logic?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/22042cf798289c1c241989bf74ad8ed14e42aef2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/d0ef0247a7919ce573a6a10a31df7bb90ab6e744.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/075004120aecd94c503c2d9301c3e6a1dba1c2e9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/640d484aba14ad7545780693dbeb20093316e70b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/94ce6b68f29b1f189c25694d3b6af197313ab177.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Suppose the <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> are events in a sample space and <img src=\"/media/ecbb38cdace112427c6f4f976dbb676d37259496.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Then which of the following statements are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/abef13dd126ce2d52ffb4325855fba04f7cc7822.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0016ba7856f8bc79a2a25d1717badf4a79462270.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/83c55f08cc0166a6727e4c6619b5ddf20ea1eb3f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/3fef0a8ecbb20d0acc9150195e90bf1a009c1ace.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following statements about informed search algorithm is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Informed search algorithm always find the optimal solution regardless of the heuristic function used.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The quality of heuristic function does not affect the performance of informed search algorithms.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Greedy Best-First Search may not find the optimal solution even with an admissible heuristic.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)<br />\n Greedy Best-First Search priorities nodes based solely on heuristic values. Which can lead to sub optimal solutions, even with admissible heuristic. This make it possible for Greedy Best-First Search to not find the optimal solution.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Identity the equivalent mathematical logic for the following statements:<br />\n “Some man are player”</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2a2354c9a17e1b5303ae83b476f98409e6181a4d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/37f5815cfad3b4762309aade81b69088f9d1f421.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/bca7c401817ad6185655517707dd960ca4669794.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/986b138d85a49087146a17326b8ae8fa92089dec.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/3621b62b85e1a22a13f186efb4581f86c2b95dae.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following adversarial search algorithm provides optimized solutions?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Megamax</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Alpha-beta pruning</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Min-max</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following is a complete heuristic search algorithm?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Beam search</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Greedy best first search</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Hill climbing search</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following statements is/are correct?<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Depth-limited search algorithm takes larger space complexity than breath first algorithm.<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Depth-limited search algorithm use the stack data structure.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following propositions is tautology?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/d3b1a25f0f0afaf17fd0524880b41aca10267766.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ff5ced3963c8f5646f490e66e59719c6cdd30b7b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Both (a) and (b)</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Neither (a) or (b)</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a15ae21753f560d545b1d43e1ab17acb8b4defee.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n In a case, 40% students study mathematics, 25% studying biology and 15% study both mathematics and biology. One student is select at random. Find the proba